<title>INDIA: Indian money market closed for bank holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian money market closed for bank holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian money market was shut on Monday as banks across the country are closed for a national holiday.</p>
<p>The market reopens on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Indian call money ended the weekend at 0.5-1.5 percent, little changed from opening quotes of 0.5-1.0 percent.</p>
</text>
